➡️ Video Description:
Text prompts alone can't give you real camera control in AI video — the camera drifts, subjects float out of frame, and you're back to rolling the dice on every generation. This video walks through the Higgsfield Blender bridge: a workflow where you block out rough 3D shapes in Blender, set your camera path, and let Higgsfield paint the realistic details on top. Five real scenes — car tracking, monster truck air time, fantasy aerial, a night chase, and a multi-room architectural cutaway — show exactly what locked camera control looks like in practice and where the workflow has limits.

